# What `docker build` must not send to the daemon.
#
# F1. This lived at `Dockerfile.dockerignore` in the repository root,
# which docker never reads: the per-Dockerfile form has to sit next to
# the Dockerfile it belongs to (`containers/be/Dockerfile.dockerignore`),
# and there is no root `Dockerfile` for the root-named one to pair with.
# So nothing was excluded from any build, ever.
#
# Measured before the fix: a 1.3 GB context — `.venv` at 319 MB,
# `portal/node_modules` at 323 MB, `.git` at 28 MB — for a Dockerfile
# that copies about 11 MB. Every build in CI and CD paid for it, and so
# did every developer.
#
# The image itself was never affected: `containers/be/Dockerfile` copies
# named paths (`./app`, `alembic`, `alembic.ini`, `pyproject.toml`,
# `uv.lock`) rather than `COPY . .`, so no secret ever reached a layer.
# This is about the upload, and about a file that looked like a control
# and was not one.
#
# A root `.dockerignore` rather than a per-Dockerfile one deliberately:
# the per-Dockerfile form is a BuildKit feature, so `DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0`
# silently ignores it — and silently ignored is how this started.

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Virtualenvs and caches
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# Node
**/node_modules
portal/dist

# Local configuration and secrets. Never copied into the image, but a
# context is uploaded to whatever daemon is building — which on a remote
# builder is not this machine.
.env
.env.*
**/*.env

# Tests, docs and tooling: not in the image, not needed to build it.
tests
docs
tools
scripts
marketplace

# …except the one file the marketplace deployer copies.
#
# F2. `marketplace/Dockerfile` is built from the repository root — its
# own instructions say so, because the chart is a sibling directory —
# and excluding `marketplace` here meant that build failed with
# "/marketplace/schema.yaml: not found". Nobody saw it, because the
# deployer image had never been built: a correct change (slimming a
# 1.3 GB context) made another artefact false, and nothing connected
# the two.
#
# A negation rather than a `marketplace/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, which
# would have been more precise and would also have reintroduced exactly
# what the note at the top of this file is about: the per-Dockerfile
# form is BuildKit-only and is silently ignored without it.
#
# The cost is 11 KB in the API image's context, which that image does
# not copy and therefore never carries.
!marketplace/schema.yaml

# …and the tool that finishes an encryption-key rotation. The runbook
# runs it inside the API container (`kubectl exec deploy/igni-api --
# python tools/rotate_secret_key.py`), and with `tools` excluded it was
# in no image: the step that re-encrypts what is stored could not be run
# where the documentation said to run it.
!tools/rotate_secret_key.py
**/*.md
**/*.log

# The other images' own build inputs.
portal
containers

# Playwright baselines, which are large and numerous.
**/*.spec.ts-snapshots
